{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A failing gate can reconstruct and expose a registered multiline credential in its excerpt, although such credentials are unusual in this configuration."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A credential crossing the output tail boundary can leave an unredacted suffix in saved gate output."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The new assertions are vacuous on every run because the verify prompt never includes the gate output they purport to check."}]}